# Copy this file to .env and fill in the values below.

# ─── Supabase (required) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# From your Supabase project's Connect dialog: the Project URL and the
# anon/publishable key. The anon key is safe to keep here — Row Level
# Security is what protects each user's data, not secrecy of this key.
# See README.md's Setup section for the one-time schema setup.
SUPABASE_URL=your_supabase_project_url_here
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your_supabase_anon_key_here

# ─── IGDB / Twitch ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The app itself no longer needs these — the Twitch Client ID + SECRET now
# live only on the server, as secrets for the `igdb` Supabase Edge Function
# (supabase/functions/igdb). Whoever deploys that function sets them with:
#
#   supabase secrets set IGDB_CLIENT_ID=... IGDB_CLIENT_SECRET=...
#
# Get both at https://dev.twitch.tv/console — create an app, then use its
# Client ID and Client Secret.
